tags.description:
Endpoints for creating, pricing, and retrieving offers for a customer's itinerary, as well as generating merchandising content for those offers.

## Merchandising SDK Integration

HTS merchandising SDKs are lightweight, embeddable components that display product offers on your website. The SDKs are built with SolidJS and delivered as web components that render in Shadow DOM with isolated styling.

### Integration Flow

```
1. Obtain SDK URL from create offer API → 2. Embed SDK in partner purchase flow → 3. Customer selects option → 4. Process selection event
```

### Custom Element

| Element Name                       |
| ---------------------------------- |
| `<hts-flights-cfar-merchandising>` |

### Basic Integration

```html
<!-- Preconnect for faster DNS resolution -->
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://hts.hopper.com" />

<!-- SDK Script (merchandising_url from create offer API response) -->
<script src="{{MERCHANDISING_URL}}" type="module" async></script>

<!-- SDK Component -->
<hts-flights-cfar-merchandising></hts-flights-cfar-merchandising>
```

### Dynamic Integration (JavaScript)

```javascript
// merchandising_url is provided in the create offer API response
const sdkUrl = merchandisingUrl;

// Create and insert script
const script = document.createElement('script');
script.src = sdkUrl;
script.type = 'module';
script.async = true;
document.head.appendChild(script);

// Create and insert component
const component = document.createElement('hts-flights-cfar-merchandising');
document.body.appendChild(component);
```

## Handling SDK Events

The SDK communicates with your page using the `postMessage` API.

### Event Types

| Event Type                  | Description                  | When Fired                                               |
| --------------------------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `hts-initialized`           | SDK loaded and ready         | On component mount                                       |
| `hts-option-selected`       | User selected an option      | When selection changes                                   |
| `hts-invalid-params`        | Invalid parameters detected  | On parameter validation failure                          |
| `hts-data-loaded`           | Offer data loaded            | After successful data parsing                            |
| `hts-dimension`             | Component dimensions changed | When size changes                                        |
| `hts-view-terms`            | User viewing terms           | When terms link is clicked                               |
| `hts-link-clicked`          | User clicked a link          | When FAQ or T&C links are clicked                        |
| `hts-initialization-failed` | Initialization blocked       | When the app cannot initialize (e.g. unsupported locale) |
| `hts-validated`             | Checkout readiness changed   | On each `hts-validate`, and on change once enabled (or immediately with `validate`)                |

### Listening to Events

```javascript
window.addEventListener('message', (event) => {
  // Verify origin for security
  if (event.origin !== 'https://hts.hopper.com') return;

  const { type, product, data } = event.data;

  switch (type) {
    case 'hts-initialized':
      console.log(`${product} SDK initialized`);
      break;
    case 'hts-option-selected':
      if (data.attached && data.offer) {
        // User selected coverage
        console.log(`Offer selected, premium: ${data.offer.premium} ${data.offer.currency}`);
      } else {
        // User declined coverage
      }
      break;
    case 'hts-invalid-params':
      console.error('SDK validation failed:', data.error);
      break;
    case 'hts-dimension':
      // Adjust iframe height if using iframe integration
      break;
    case 'hts-link-clicked':
      // contextType is "faq" or "termsAndConditions"
      break;
    case 'hts-initialization-failed':
      // Widget will not render — hide container and do not require selection
      console.warn('SDK initialization failed:', data.type);
      break;
    case 'hts-validated':
      // Enable/disable your proceed control based on data.isValid
      setProceedEnabled(data.isValid);
      break;
  }
});
```

### Key Event Payloads

#### `hts-option-selected`

```json
{
  "type": "hts-option-selected",
  "product": "flights-cfar",
  "data": {
    "attached": true,
    "selected": "0018868d-652f-4134-b094-a37ebb651f1a",
    "offer": {
      "offerId": "0018868d-652f-4134-b094-a37ebb651f1a",
      "premium": "48.00",
      "currency": "USD",
      "coveragePercentage": "100"
    }
  }
}
```

When `attached` is `false`, the user declined the offer.

#### `hts-initialization-failed`

```json
{
  "type": "hts-initialization-failed",
  "product": "flights-cfar",
  "data": {
    "type": "unsupported_locale",
    "locale": "ja"
  }
}
```

Fired when the app cannot initialize due to a precondition failure. The widget will not render. Currently the only failure type is `unsupported_locale`, indicating the tenant is configured to reject unsupported locales rather than falling back to English.

#### `hts-validated`

Tells you whether it is safe to proceed to checkout. Use it to enable/disable your proceed/checkout control.

**When it fires.** `hts-validated` is not emitted on load — this event stays quiet until you opt in (other widget events still fire as normal). It starts emitting the first time either you send an `hts-validate` ingress event (e.g. when the customer attempts to proceed), or you set the `validate` attribute/parameter on the component (see the Component Attributes / Iframe Parameters tables below). From then on it emits the **current** `isValid` whenever the value changes (this automatic stream is de-duplicated). In addition, **every `hts-validate` you send always responds with a fresh `hts-validated`** carrying the current validity — even when it hasn't changed — so you can re-query readiness at any time; that ingress also re-shows the in-widget "selection required" prompt.

```json
{
  "type": "hts-validated",
  "product": "flights-cfar",
  "data": { "isValid": false }
}
```

**How to interpret `isValid`:** Treat `isValid: false` as "disable proceed," **not** "show an error." If you want a checkout-readiness signal at load without any customer action, set `validate`; the first `hts-validated` then reflects the offer's selection mode (a forced-choice widget starts `isValid: false`; one that permits no selection starts `isValid: true`). Otherwise drive validation from the proceed attempt: send `hts-validate` and read the resulting `hts-validated`. Surface validation messaging only at the proceed attempt (`hts-validate` and/or your own copy).

## Component Attributes

When using the web component, customizations are set as **kebab-case** attributes on the custom element.

| Attribute            | Type   | Description                                              |
| -------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `selected`           | string | Pre-select an option (`none`, or an offer id)           |
| `validate`      | boolean | Emit `hts-validated` (current validity) as soon as this attribute is set — on load or later — instead of staying silent until the first `hts-validate`. Default `false`. |
| `rewards-type`       | string | Override rewards type                                   |
| `rewards-conversion` | string | Override rewards conversion                             |
| `entry-point`        | string | The placement the widget is shown in; adjusts UI & copy |

```html
<hts-flights-cfar-merchandising
  selected="none"
  rewards-type="miles"
  rewards-conversion="100"
  entry-point="postbooking"
></hts-flights-cfar-merchandising>

<!-- Pre-select a specific offer -->
<hts-flights-cfar-merchandising selected="0018868d-..."></hts-flights-cfar-merchandising>
```

## Iframe Parameters

When using iframe integration, the same customizations are supplied as **camelCase** query parameters on the merchandising URL. See the _Iframe Integration (Alternative)_ section below for the embed snippet.

| Parameter           | Type   | Description                                              |
| ------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `selected`          | string | Pre-select an option (`none`, or an offer id)           |
| `validate`      | boolean | Emit `hts-validated` (current validity) from load instead of staying silent until the first `hts-validate`. Default `false`. |
| `rewardsType`       | string | Override rewards type                                   |
| `rewardsConversion` | string | Override rewards conversion                             |
| `entryPoint`        | string | The placement the widget is shown in; adjusts UI & copy |

## Iframe Integration (Alternative)

For partners who prefer iframe-based integration, use the `merchandising_url` from the create offer response:

```html
<iframe
  src="{{MERCHANDISING_URL}}"
  style="width: 100%; border: none; height: 400px;">
</iframe>
```

Use the `hts-dimension` event to adjust iframe height dynamically.

## Loading Tolerance

If the `hts-initialized` event is not received within a reasonable tolerance period after embedding the SDK, the hosting application should hide the widget and not require forced selection. This prevents user experience degradation if the SDK fails to load.

## Styling and Theming

The SDK renders in Shadow DOM with partner-specific themes applied automatically based on your `partnerId`. Internal component styling cannot be overridden due to Shadow DOM encapsulation. Contact HTS if you need theme customization.

## Security Considerations

- **Origin Verification**: Always verify `event.origin` when handling postMessage events
- **HTTPS Only**: Always use HTTPS URLs in production
- **CSP Headers**: Ensure your Content Security Policy allows loading scripts from `hts.hopper.com`

## Alternative: Merchandising Contents API

Partners who cannot embed the widget can use the **Create Offer Merchandising Contents** endpoint to retrieve product copy and messaging as JSON. This approach requires the partner to build their own UI while using HTS-provided content.
